 the root question — for which capsid–receptor binding signatures transcytosis occurs — specifically whether a shared interface motif marks transcytosis-competent complexes.\\\",\\\"compute_open\\\":\\\"More parallel compute would buy model runs (capsid × receptor × pose); published measurements of its effect stop at single-digit numbers of AAV–receptor complexes modeled per study — two LRP6 peptide complexes in https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518 — and above that it is unknown whether exhaustive enumeration would surface a shared transcytosis-competent motif or demonstrate that no such motif exists.\\\",\\\"sequential\\\":\\\"none: every capsid–receptor pair is an independent docking or AlphaFold-Multimer job with its own random seeds, so the work already splits into independent pieces.\\\",\\\"source_urls\\\":[\\\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518\\\",\\\"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_2024_FINAL_Ishan.pdf\\\",\\\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079\\\"]}. Root question: Can molecular mapping of AAV capsid-receptor interactions on brain microvascular endothelial cells determine which AAV variants transcytose across the blood-brain barrier versus remain intracellular, and for which capsid-receptor binding signatures?. Read only pages you fetch and what you write under /home/hal/dev/interp/metis/experiments/blind-01/20261021-0116-loop/out/r0/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/55c57ced; write only under /home/hal/dev/interp/metis/experiments/blind-01/20261021-0116-loop/out/r0/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/55c57ced. When the plan is written, return it as the record in your output schema; producer.md stays your working file. In the record, put every number the cost or the size of the test depends on in numbers, each with a basis: CITED (a page states this number for this same setting; give the page text that shows it), PROXY (a page states it for a different model, GPU, dataset, size 