    "reasoning_content": "Let me break down this task carefully.\n\nI need to:\n1. Read the option record (given in the prompt)\n2. Research relevant sources (fetch pages cited, and maybe search the web)\n3. Write a producer.md working file under the specified directory\n4. Return a JSON record matching the schema\n\nKey constraints:\n- Write only under `/home/hal/dev/interp/metis/experiments/blind-01/20261021-0116-loop/out/r0/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/55c57ced`\n- Read only pages I fetch and what I write under that dir\n- Cite URLs for every factual claim\n- Numbers need basis: CITED, PROXY, MEASURED, DERIVED, DESIGN, GUESS\n- Budget: up to $1,000 GPU credit at Lambda on-demand prices\n- Return only JSON, no other text\n\nLet me start by exploring the working directory and fetching the cited sources.\n\nThe option: Exhaustive capsid–receptor complex enumeration (docking and AlphaFold-Multimer) against BBB receptor panel (LY6A, LY6C1, ALPL, LRP6, CA4, AAVR) with engineered capsid libraries.\n\nI need to make it concrete: what to build, baseline, how to check it's right, cost.\n\nLet me plan the work:\n\n1. First, look at the working directory structure\n2. Fetch the three source URLs:\n   - https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518 (AlphaFold-Multimer models of LRP6 with AAV-X1 and CAP-Mac VR-VIII peptides)\n   - https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_2024_FINAL_Ishan.pdf (Voyager poster)\n   - https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079 (~150 AAV capsid structures catalog)\n3. Search for more sources: AlphaFold-Multimer compute requirements, ColabFold runtime, docking tools (HDOCK, ClusPro), AAV capsid structures (PDB), Lambda pricing page4. Design the experiment:\n   - Capsid library: e.g., AAV9, AAV-X1, AAVrh.10, PHP.B, PHP.eB, AAV2, AAV8, CAP-Mac, etc. — maybe use known engineered variants\n   - Receptor panel: LY6A, LY6C1, ALPL, LRP6, CA4, AAVR (6 receptors) — GPI-anchored: LY6A, LY6C1, ALPL, CA4; LRP6