eceptor pose models\". Prior: 10 models (5 per peptide × 2 peptides). Quote is exact from the figure caption. \n- Capsid panel details (Table 1): AAV9, AAV.CAP-B10, AAV.CAP-B22, AAV-MaCPNS1, AAV-MaCPNS2, AAV.CAP-Mac, AAV9-X1.1, AAV-BI30. VR-IV AA452-458, VR-VIII AA587-590 modifications. This is a GREAT concrete capsid library: 8 capsids with BBB/CNS phenotypes and known receptor interactions (LRP6 for CAP-Mac and X1.1; LY6A for CAP-B22; AAVR for all except MaCPNS1).\n- Receptor interactions table (Table 2): AAV9→IL3; CAP-B22→LY6A, FAM234A; CAP-Mac→LRP6, GP2; AAV9-X1.1→LRP6, GP2. All→AAVR (from text: \"all except MaCPNS1 exhibited detectable AAVR binding\").\n- \"These cross-links place IL3's interaction site with AAV9 near the base of the threefold symmetry spike and the twofold symmetry depression...\"\n- AAVR PKD2 binding: \"For AAV1, -2, -9, and PHP.eB, the PKD2 domain of AAVR interacted with the capsids in the same binding mode, along the side of the 3-fold protrusions and on top of the 2/5-fold wall (Fig. 7C)\" — from PMC12682079.\n- LRP6 domains: \"the LRP6 extracellular domain contains 4 YWTD domains (E1-E4)\"; \"LRP6-E1E2 but not LRP6-E3E4\"; \"sub-nM apparent affinity\" for LRP6-Fc binding.\n- SPR: AAV9-X1.1 and CAP-Mac bind human LRP6-Fc with \"sub-nM apparent affinity\".\n- \"AAV9, on the other hand, bound only to AAVR's PKD2\".\n\nFrom PMC12682079 (Hsi-Bell et al. 2025, open access):\n- \"To date, 155 AAV capsid structures at a resolution ≤ 4 Å have been determined since 2002\"\n- \"a library of currently ∼150 high-resolution AAV capsid structures, with more than 50% determined in the last 5 years alone\"\n- AAV capsid: T=1, diameter ~25 nm; 60 VP monomers; VP3 ~520 C-terminal aa ordered.\n- \"VR-IV, -V, and -VIII interact with each other to form the 3-fold protrusions; and VR-VI and -VII are located at the base of the 3-fold protrusions.\"\n- CA4: \"Another membrane protein complexed with an AAV capsid is carbonic anhydrase 4 (Car4). This protein is anchored to the cell surface via a glycosylphosphatidylinositol linkage, which was identified as a potential receptor for the engineered capsids AAV9-P31 and AAV9-P36. Recombinant Car4 was found to bind to the 3-fold protrusions of AAV9-P31. Due to its size, similar to antibodies bound close to the symmetry axis, a localized cryo-EM reconstruction approach was needed to resolve the complex at 1.8 Å resolution.\"\n  → CA4 binds 3-fold protrusions of AAV9-P31 — a GPI-anchored receptor at the 3-fold! This is direct support for the motif hypothesis. And there's a structure (1.8 Å).\n- AAVR: \"Constructs comprising PKD1-5 or PKD1-2 have been complexed with the capsids of AAV1, -2, -5, -9, AAVgo.1, and the engineered capsid PHP.eB ... cryo-EM structures ... resolutions ranging from 2.4 to 3.8 Å. For AAV1, -2, -9, and PHP.eB, the PKD2 domain of AAVR interacted with the capsids in the same binding mode, along the side of the 3-fold protrusions and on top of the 2/5-fold wall\"\n- PDB IDs mentioned: AAV2 (8FYW), AAV5 (7KP3), AAVrh.8 (4RSO), AAVhu.37 (6U95), AAV9-Fab (9B6O), AAV8-AAVX (9DC3), AAV2-AAVR (6NZ0), AAV1-SIA (5EGC).\n- Interface areas for antibodies ~1000-2000 Å² (avg ~1500).\n\nThis is excellent. The option's receptor panel: LY6A, LY6C1, ALPL, LRP6, CA4, AAVR. The poster (Voyager) is cited for \"3-fold-axis engagement of GPI-anchored receptors\". Let me fetch the poster now. Also need:\n1. Lambda pricing page (for quotes).\n2. AlphaFold-Multimer/ColabFold runtime benchmarks.\n3. GROMACS throughput.\n4. Maybe the CA4/AAV9-P31 paper for phenotype labels.\n5. LY6A/PHP.B open-access paper for phenotype labels.\n6. LY6C1 and ALPL as AAV receptors — which papers? Let me search. LY6C1 was identified as a receptor for AAV9? Hmm — there's a 2024/2025 paper \"LY6C1 is a receptor for AAV9 mediating BBB transcytosis\"? And ALPL (alkaline phosphatase, GPI-anchored) was identified as an AAV receptor in some screen? Let me search.\n\nThe Voyager poster: \"POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_2024_